{"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Binary-decision-diagrams","title":"Binary decision diagrams","identifiers":["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram"]},{"anchor":"Zero-suppressed-decision-diagrams","title":"Zero-suppressed decision diagrams","identifiers":["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram"]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/decisiondiagrams"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"DecisionDiagrams"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"DecisionDiagrams","externalID":"DecisionDiagrams","symbolKind":"module"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a table of reduced ordered binary decision diagrams (Bryant,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1986). Each function is a directed acyclic graph whose vertices test variables in index order,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with a low child for the variable false and a high child for true, down to the constants. No two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices test the same variable with the same children, and none has equal children, so each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"function has exactly one root, and checking whether two functions are equal is comparing roots."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import DecisionDiagrams","","var diagram = BinaryDecisionDiagram(variableCount: 3)","let x0 = diagram.variable(0), x1 = diagram.variable(1), x2 = diagram.variable(2)","let f = diagram.or(diagram.and(x0, x1), x2)   \/\/ x0 ∧ x1 ∨ x2","diagram.satisfyingAssignmentCount(of: f)       \/\/ 5","diagram.anySatisfyingAssignment(of: f)         \/\/ [false, false, true]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The diagram of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"f"},{"type":"text","text":" has five vertices: three tests and the two constants. Following the low edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"means the variable is false, the high edge that it is true."}]},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Vertex","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tests"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Low child","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"High child"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"root"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x0"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the test of "},{"code":"x2","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the test of "},{"code":"x1","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x1"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the test of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x2"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"true","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x2"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"false"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"true"}]}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The test of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x2"},{"type":"text","text":" is shared: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x0"},{"type":"text","text":" false and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x0 ∧ ¬x1"},{"type":"text","text":" both leave "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"f"},{"type":"text","text":" equal to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x2"},{"type":"text","text":", so both lead"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the one vertex that stands for it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Functions combine under any of the sixteen binary operators with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/apply(_:_:_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" in O(|","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"f"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":"| |","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"g"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":"|), through a computed table of results","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"already found. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/restrict(_:variable:to:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" fixes a variable, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/exists(_:in:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/forall(_:in:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" quantify","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"over variables. The table’s vertices are a ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/graphView-swift.property","type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so Grafluent’s traversals and drawings run over a function’s diagram from its root.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram"},{"type":"text","text":" is a table of families of sets (Minato, 1993). Its vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"test elements in index order, with a low child for the sets without the element and a high child"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for those with it. In place of the rule that removes a vertex with equal children, it removes one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose high child is the empty family, so an element no set contains never appears in a diagram,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a sparse family over many elements stays small."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var diagram = ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram(elementCount: 3)","let f = diagram.family([[0, 1], [1, 2], [2]])","diagram.count(of: f)                                 \/\/ 3","diagram.minimalSets(of: diagram.including(2, in: f)) \/\/ {{2}}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Families combine by ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/union(_:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/intersection(_:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/subtracting(_:from:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", and set by set by","type":"text"},{"text":